From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Friedrich <261542475+aeries0x@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:40:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] phy: apple: atc: enable the dummy PHY on T8132
 SuperSpeed ports

The T8132 PIPE lock that starts the routing to USB3 is only acknowledged
while PIPEHANDLER_DUMMY_PHY_EN is set, as on T8122. The driver never sets
it on T8132 and relies on the boot firmware: on the J604 (MacBook Pro
14" M4) iBoot leaves it set on ATC0 and ATC1 but not on ATC3, the right
port. There the first USB3 start fails and leaves the port without USB:

  phy-apple-atc 41aa90000.phy: Pipehandler lock not acked.
  dwc3-apple 41a280000.usb: USB3 PHY setup failed, err=-110
  sn201202x 2-0c: failed to place Type-C mux in safe mode: -5

with PIPEHANDLER_NONSELECTED_OVERRIDE reading 0x1332 on ATC3 against
0x9332 on ATC0 and ATC1. Set the bit when the PIPE handler is set up on a
port with its SuperSpeed banks, at probe and after the power domain was
off, so the port no longer depends on what the boot firmware left.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Friedrich <261542475+aeries0x@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit fb2094f94a0151ef3134d7fed9ba364055565c02)
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/phy/apple/atc.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
index 27a047e69f..fd10bd6191 100644
--- a/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/apple/atc.c
@@ -2087,6 +2087,15 @@ static void atcphy_setup_pipehandler(struct apple_atcphy *atcphy)
 		      PIPEHANDLER_T8132_USB2_CONFIG_EN);
 		atcphy_pipehandler_set_mux(atcphy, PIPEHANDLER_MUX_CTRL_DATA_DUMMY,
 					   PIPEHANDLER_MUX_CTRL_CLK_DUMMY);
+		/*
+		 * As on T8122, the PIPE lock that starts the routing to USB3
+		 * is only acknowledged with the dummy PHY enabled. The boot
+		 * firmware leaves it set on the ports it brought up, but not
+		 * on every SuperSpeed port: on the J604, ATC3 comes up with it
+		 * clear and its first USB3 start times out.
+		 */
+		if (atcphy->t8132_ss)
+			atcphy_enable_dummy_phy(atcphy);
 		atcphy->pipe_state = ATCPHY_PIPEHANDLER_STATE_DUMMY;
 		atcphy->pipe_pending = false;
 		return;
